## What FBE.6b surfaced (foldback-reopening findings)

### BLOCKER-FBE6b.1 — README + getting-started.md `loam init .` does not match CLI's required `--from` flag

The README's literal install (`pip install -r install-from-source.txt`
followed by `loam init .`) FAILS at step 3 because `loam init` requires
`--from CANONICAL_SOURCE` (an absolute POSIX path or http(s)/git@ URL)
but the README provides no `--from` flag. A stranger following the
README literally gets `loam init: error: the following arguments are
required: --from` (exit code 2).

The CLI source confirms `--from` is required: `framework/loam-init/
src/loam/loam_init/cli.py:186-187` (`required=True`). The CLI's
help text shows `--from CANONICAL_SOURCE` is required.

The CLI works correctly when `--from` is provided (the FBE.6b smoke
verifies this with `loam init <ws> --from <repo>`). The bug is in
the README + getting-started.md not specifying `--from`.

This is the same SHAPE of bug FBE.6's BLOCKER-FBE6.1 was: docs
describe a flow that does not match what the CLI accepts. FBE.8
fixed the install flow but did not fix the `loam init .` invocation
— both docs still say `loam init .` (zero `--from`).

ODD §2.5 framing: the README's documented contract (install →
`loam init .` works) is not satisfied by the actual code path the
README describes.

Fix shape: either doc-only (FBE.9 Path A: update README + getting-
started.md to use `loam init . --from .` or similar), OR CLI-side
(FBE.9 Path B: make `--from` optional and default to pwd if it's a
git tree). Path B recommended (single-fence amendment at loam-init;
shrinks doc/CLI surface mismatch).

### HIGH-FBE6b.1 — Pervasive `Amendment #N` source-comment references

A stranger reading source code post-install sees pervasive references
to internal amendment numbers (339 occurrences across 95 files in
synth). Concrete examples: `Amendment #20 — Site 6...`, `Amendment
#26 — teardown CDC 2...`, `Amendment #28 — defence in depth...`,
`amendment #67 (AC.SFR.3)...`. NOT in the AC.M11a.2 banned list
(which specifies `pos-amend`, `loam-amend`, `loam-mode`, `docs/
rebuild/`, `odd-methodology`, `odd-in-loam`, `duration-estimation-
rubric`, `pos-publish-framework-only`); same shape as the original
loam-user-review LOW-3 finding ("dev-vocabulary leakage in pyproject
descriptions") but at much larger scale and across source code
rather than packaging metadata.

Severity HIGH not BLOCKER: not first-run-visible (strangers don't
typically read installed-package source code as part of first-run);
install + first-`claude`-session UX doesn't expose this surface.
But anyone debugging an issue and tracing through code will see
internal amendment numbers throughout.

Fix shape: defer to v0.1.x dedicated source-comment scrub amendment.
Document as known issue at v0.1.0 GO (release notes "known
limitations" section). Builder's call whether to combine into FBE.9
alongside BLOCKER-FBE6b.1 or defer.

